{"availability":"available","full":"PegasusXLab/main","name":"main","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-10T01:15:59Z","updated":"2026-10-11T07:26:45Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://main-six-lemon-62.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://galleriverse.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:49.861Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:49.861Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:49.861Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T07:26:49.861Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Galleriverse lets creators with no coding or 3D experience build an immersive gallery for their art. They draw rooms on a simple 2D floor plan, set each room's colours, lighting and sound, and hang artwork with titles and stories on the walls. Galleriverse compiles that layout into a 3D gallery that anyone can walk through from a shared link, on a laptop or a phone, with no account needed. The editor is the product; the 3D gallery is what it produces. Built for Hacklanta 2026 (Adobe Creative track)."],"features":["2D floor plan editor: rectangular rooms on a 1 m grid; add neighbours with directional + buttons, drag, resize, snap, and undo/redo (Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Shift+Z).","Three editor views: 2D, 3D POV (the real visitor tour, rendered from the live unsaved gallery), and Top-down (orbit overview).","Rooms with character: wall colour, floor finish, lighting presets, and atmosphere presets (Gallery White, Golden Hour, Neon Bunker, Moonlit, Custom) that blend as you move between rooms.","A gallery-grade look: image-based lighting, picture lights over each artwork, ceilings, baseboards, soft corner shading, textured wood/concrete/marble floors, and framed, matted artwork.","Artwork with stories: upload images (resized in the browser), add title, artist and story; visitors click a frame to read its plaque."],"sour